+# Risk Mitigation & Hardenings
+
+This patch implements operational mitigations for the key risk areas:
+
+- Poisoning / runaway auto‑retrain loops:
+  - retrain_guard.py enforces curated example requirement, cooldowns and rate limits
+  - OPA policy (risk_mitigation.rego) encodes high-level checks and requires human sign-off for sensitive datasets
+  - multisig_verify.py supports verifying multi-party approvals (cosign wrapper)
+
+- DP outages / miscounting:
+  - PrometheusRule (dp_alerts.yaml) alerts on DP service downtime and high charge failure rates
+  - OPA policy gates block/requires human decision when DP indicates unavailable
+
+- Over‑automation for high‑impact models:
+  - OPA rules require human sign-off for high sensitivity models and production promotions
+  - multisig helper supports multi-party cosign verification for approvals (used by retrain_guard)
+
+- LRM jailbreaks and tool exfiltration:
+  - safety_stream_checker_v2.py improves streaming heuristics and checks retrieval provenance
+  - jailed executor scanner (scan_and_return.py) redacts and blocks secrets and stores signed evidence bundles
+  - strong_lrm_tests.py expands red-team coverage to multi-stage jailbreaks, tool-exfil and RAG poison simulations
+
+Integration notes:
+- Orchestrator should call retrain_guard.py prior to submitting auto-retrain Argo workflows.
+- The retrain_guard records retrain history into a local state file (can be replaced by Redis for HA).
+- For production, replace the state backend with Redis / DynamoDB to ensure concurrency-safe counters.
+- Provide COSIGN_KMS_URI and ensure cosign is installed on nodes that run multisig verification.
+- Wire Prometheus to load dp_alerts.yaml and configure the dp-service job label.
+
